<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH OAKS RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH OAKS RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-07-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the group one Irish</p>
<p>Oaks for three-year-old fillies, run over one and a half miles</p>
<p>(2.4 kms) at The Curragh on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Ebadiyla 9-2 (ridden by John Murtagh)</p>
<p>2. Yashmak 6-4 favourite (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>3. Brilliance 5-1 (Sylvain Guillot)</p>
<p>11 ran</p>
<p>Distances: 3 lengths, head.</p>
<p>Winner owned by The Aga Khan and trained in Ireland by John</p>
<p>Oxx.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 112,700 sterling ($191,000)</p>
